<PageTitle>Blazor Forms and Validation — FlexCore</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Forms" Category="Components" CategoryHref="components" ControlName="FormControl"
                   Tagline="A form generated from a model or laid out by hand, with data-annotation validation, groups, templates and tooltips."
                   SourcePath="Forms/FormControl.razor;Forms/FormItemControl.razor;Forms/FormAutoGeneratedItemsControl.razor;Forms/FormGroupControl.razor;Forms/ValidationTooltipControl.razor;Forms/ValidationMessageControl.razor;Forms/ValidationSummaryControl.razor;Forms/FormModels.cs;PropertyGridControl.razor">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>FormControl</code> wraps Blazor's <code>EditForm</code> around a <code>Model</code> or an <code>EditContext</code> you supply.
            Without child content it generates one <code>FormItemControl</code> per supported property of the model; with child content you
            place the items yourself, grouped in <code>FormGroupControl</code> fieldsets, spanning columns, or replaced by your own editor through
            a template. Each item picks its editor from the property type, parses what is typed into that type, reports a parse failure as a
            validation message, and tells the form about every accepted value. Submit runs the data-annotation validator and raises either
            <code>OnValidSubmit</code> or <code>OnInvalidSubmit</code>; <code>ValidationTooltipControl</code> shows a field's messages in a
            tooltip on hover or focus.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="generated" Title="Generated form" RazorCode="@Code.Generated" CSharpCode="@Code.GeneratedCs">
            <Description><p>One line of markup; the ten properties of the model decide the rest. <code>Display</code> sets the captions and the order and hides the id, <code>Editable(false)</code> makes the reference read-only, the enum and the nullable bool become dropdowns, the date carries a time because of its <code>DataType</code>, and the time picker comes from <code>TimeOnly</code>. Clear the name or type 25 as the quantity and press Save: the summary and the field messages come from the <code>Required</code>, <code>MinLength</code> and <code>Range</code> attributes. Type letters into the quantity and the item itself reports the parse failure.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <FormControl Model="@_order" Columns="2" OnValidSubmit="OrderSaved" OnInvalidSubmit="OrderInvalid" />
                <p class="result">@_orderStatus</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="handbuilt" Title="Hand-built form: group, template, tooltip, buttons" RazorCode="@Code.Handbuilt" CSharpCode="@Code.HandbuiltCs">
            <Description><p>The same control with its own child content. A <code>FormGroupControl</code> frames the contact fields two across, and City reaches into a nested object through a dotted <code>Field</code>. Quantity swaps its editor for a template whose buttons set the value through the field context; take it to 0 and Send to see the range message under it. The "Name rules" text is a <code>ValidationTooltipControl</code>: after an invalid Send, hover or focus it to read Name's messages. The buttons are a <code>ButtonsTemplate</code>: Send submits, Check calls <code>IsValid()</code> without submitting. The line below is fed by <code>OnUpdate</code>, which fires for every accepted value.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <FormControl @ref="_form" Model="@_enquiry" Columns="2" ShowValidationSummary="false"
                             OnValidSubmit="EnquirySent" OnInvalidSubmit="EnquiryInvalid" OnUpdate='a => _last = $"{a.Field} = {a.Value}"'>
                    <ChildContent>
                        <FormGroupControl Label="Contact" Columns="2">
                            <FormItemControl Field="Name" />
                            <FormItemControl Field="Email" />
                            <FormItemControl Field="Address.City" Label="City" />
                            <ValidationTooltipControl Field="Name"><span class="rules">Name rules</span></ValidationTooltipControl>
                        </FormGroupControl>
                        <FormItemControl Field="Quantity" Hint="A template replaces the editor; the field context sets the value.">
                            <Template Context="field">
                                <div class="stepper">
                                    <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="() => field.SetValueAsync((int)field.Value! - 1)">−</ButtonControl>
                                    <strong>@field.Value</strong>
                                    <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="() => field.SetValueAsync((int)field.Value! + 1)">+</ButtonControl>
                                </div>
                            </Template>
                        </FormItemControl>
                        <FormItemControl Field="Notes" EditorType="FormEditorType.TextArea" Rows="4" />
                    </ChildContent>
                    <ButtonsTemplate>
                        <ButtonControl ButtonType="submit">Send</ButtonControl>
                        <ButtonControl OnClick='() => _enquiryStatus = _form!.IsValid() ? "Valid." : "Not valid yet."'>Check</ButtonControl>
                    </ButtonsTemplate>
                </FormControl>
                <p class="result">@_enquiryStatus Last change: @_last</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="property-grid" Title="Property grid: edit an object" RazorCode="@Code.PropertyGrid" CSharpCode="@Code.PropertyGridCs" CssCode="@Code.PropertyGridCss">
            <Description><p>A property grid suits a settings or inspector panel: each public property with a getter and a setter becomes a name and editor row, every edit is written to the object as it is made, and there is no submit button and no data-annotation validation. The generated form above fits an object someone fills in and saves, with captions, order and validation taken from its attributes. Here Package Code is read-only through <code>[Editable(false)]</code>, and <code>Summary</code> has no setter, so it gets no row; the line below prints it. Season as buttons sets <code>CustomEditor</code>, which replaces the editor in every row, so the fragment draws Season as a button group and hands every other property to a <code>FormItemControl</code>, the editor the grid renders when <code>CustomEditor</code> is not set.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                <ToggleButtonControl @bind-Selected="_seasonButtons">Season as buttons</ToggleButtonControl>
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <div class="tour-grid">
                    @if (!_seasonButtons)
                    {
                        <PropertyGridControl TModel="TourPackage" Value="@_package" ValueChanged="PackageChanged" />
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <PropertyGridControl TModel="TourPackage" Value="@_package">
                            <CustomEditor Context="row">
                                @if (row.Prop.Name == nameof(TourPackage.Season))
                                {
                                    <ButtonGroupControl Items="@Seasons" Values="@(new[] { _package.Season.ToString() })" ValuesChanged="SeasonChanged" AriaLabel="Season" />
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <FormItemControl Model="@row.Model" Field="@row.Prop.Name" ShowLabel="false" ValueChanged="PackageChanged" />
                                }
                            </CustomEditor>
                        </PropertyGridControl>
                    }
                </div>
                <p class="result">@_package.Summary Changes reported: @_changes.</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-formcontrol-parameters" Title="FormControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Form.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="FormControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Form" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-formcontrol-events" Title="FormControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.FormEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="FormControl events" Rows="Vocab.FormEvents" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-formcontrol-methods" Title="FormControl methods" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.FormMethods.Length, "methods")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="FormControl methods" Rows="Vocab.FormMethods" />
                <p>
                <code>CurrentEditContext</code> exposes the context in use. <code>CssClass</code>, <code>Style</code>, <code>Id</code>,
                <code>Visible</code>, <code>Enabled</code> and <code>AdditionalAttributes</code> come from <code>FlexControlBase</code> and apply to the
                <code>form</code> element; <code>Enabled="false"</code> disables the submit button, <code>SubmitAsync</code> and every item.
                </p>
                <p>Without child content the form generates an item for each property of the model that:</p>
                <ul>
                <li>is public, readable and not an indexer;</li>
                <li>has a supported type, or its nullable form: an enum, <code>string</code>, <code>bool</code>, <code>Guid</code>, <code>DateTime</code>, <code>DateOnly</code>, <code>TimeOnly</code>, <code>decimal</code>, <code>double</code>, <code>float</code> or any integer type;</li>
                <li>is not marked <code>[Display(AutoGenerateField = false)]</code>.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Items follow <code>[Display(Order = n)]</code>; properties without an order come last, in declaration order.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-formitemcontrol-parameters" Title="FormItemControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Item.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="FormItemControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Item" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-formitemcontrol-events" Title="FormItemControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.ItemEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="FormItemControl events" Rows="Vocab.ItemEvents" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-formitemcontrol-methods" Title="FormItemControl methods" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.ItemMethods.Length, "methods")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="FormItemControl methods" Rows="Vocab.ItemMethods" />
                <p>The editor is chosen in this order:</p>
                <ol>
                <li><code>Template</code>, when set.</li>
                <li>A dropdown for <code>EditorType.DropDownList</code>, for an enum, or for a nullable <code>bool</code>. Choices are <code>Options</code>, else the enum names or True and False, with a blank entry first for a nullable property.</li>
                <li>A switch for <code>EditorType.Switch</code>.</li>
                <li>A checkbox for <code>bool</code>.</li>
                <li>A date picker for <code>DateTime</code> and <code>DateOnly</code>; it shows the time when <code>ShowTime</code> is set or the property carries <code>[DataType(DataType.DateTime)]</code>.</li>
                <li>A time picker for <code>TimeOnly</code>.</li>
                <li>A text box for everything else; <code>EditorType.TextArea</code> makes it multi-line with <code>Rows</code> lines.</li>
                </ol>
                <p>
                Asking for <code>Switch</code> or <code>CheckBox</code> on a property that is not a <code>bool</code>, <code>DatePicker</code> on one that is
                not a date, or <code>TimePicker</code> on one that is not a <code>TimeOnly</code> throws. Text is converted to the property type with
                <code>Culture</code>; an empty value becomes null for a nullable property; a value that does not convert leaves the property unchanged and
                adds "Enter a valid <em>caption</em>." to the context, and a null for a non-nullable value type adds "<em>Caption</em> is required."
                The caption is <code>Label</code>, else <code>[Display(Name)]</code>, else the property name split at its capitals. An item is editable
                only while it and its form are enabled, the property has a public setter and it is not marked <code>[Editable(false)]</code>.
                <code>FormEditorType</code> is <code>Auto</code>, <code>TextBox</code>, <code>TextArea</code>, <code>CheckBox</code>, <code>Switch</code>,
                <code>DatePicker</code>, <code>TimePicker</code> or <code>DropDownList</code>; <code>FormFieldChangedArgs(object Model, string Field, object? Value)</code>
                is the record both <code>ValueChanged</code> and <code>OnUpdate</code> receive.
                </p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-formfieldcontext-passed-to-a-template" Title="FormFieldContext, passed to a Template" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Ctx.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="FormFieldContext, passed to a Template" Rows="Vocab.Ctx" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-formgroupcontrol-parameters" Title="FormGroupControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Group.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="FormGroupControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Group" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-validationtooltipcontrol-parameters" Title="ValidationTooltipControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Tooltip.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="ValidationTooltipControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Tooltip" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-validationmessagecontrol-parameters" Title="ValidationMessageControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Message.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="ValidationMessageControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Message" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-validationsummarycontrol-parameters" Title="ValidationSummaryControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Summary.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="ValidationSummaryControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Summary" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-classes" Title="CSS classes" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Css.Length, "classes")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.Css" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-propertygridcontrol" Title="PropertyGridControl" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Grid.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="PropertyGridControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Grid" />
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="Editor by property type" Rows="Vocab.GridEditors" />
                <p>
                The rows are the public instance properties of the object's runtime type that have a getter and a setter and are not indexers, in the
                order <code>GetProperties</code> returns them; a property whose setter is not public still gets a row, with a disabled editor. The name
                column is the property name split at its capitals, so <code>PricePerPerson</code> shows as Price Per Person. The grid reads no attributes
                itself: <code>[Display]</code>, <code>[Category]</code>, <code>[Description]</code> and <code>[Browsable]</code> neither rename, group,
                describe nor hide a row. Each editor is a <code>FormItemControl</code> with its label hidden, so it still honours <code>[Editable(false)]</code>
                and <code>[DataType(DataType.DateTime)]</code>, and uses <code>[Display(Name)]</code> as the editor's accessible name and in its messages.
                There is no data-annotation validator, so <code>[Required]</code>, <code>[Range]</code> and the like are not checked; text that does not
                convert leaves the property unchanged and shows "Enter a valid <em>caption</em>." under the editor.
                </p>
                <p>
                The markup is an <code>fx-propertygrid</code> div around an <code>fx-propertygrid-table</code>; each row is an
                <code>fx-propertygrid-name</code> cell and an <code>fx-propertygrid-editor</code> cell. A <code>bool</code> row's checkbox also shows the
                caption beside the box; the example's CSS hides that copy visually and keeps it as the checkbox's accessible name.
                </p>
            </DocSection>
        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <p>
            Each item's label is tied to its editor: a text box is labelled by the visible label, or by <code>aria-label</code> when the label is
            hidden, points at its message area with <code>aria-describedby</code> and sets <code>aria-invalid</code> while it has messages; the
            dropdowns, pickers and checkboxes receive the caption as their own label. Validation messages and the summary have
            <code>role="alert"</code>. The tooltip host is focusable, labelled "Validation details" by default, and names its tooltip through
            <code>aria-describedby</code>, so the messages are reachable with Tab as well as by hovering.
        </p>
        <p>
            <code>PropertyGridControl</code> is a two-column table without header cells, and its name cell is plain text rather than a
            <code>label</code>. Each built-in editor still receives the row's caption as its accessible name through <code>FormItemControl</code>:
            <code>aria-label</code> on the text box, the caption as the dropdown's and pickers' label, and the checkbox's own label. A conversion
            message has <code>role="alert"</code>. The grid adds no keys of its own; Tab moves through the enabled editors in row order. An editor
            drawn by <code>CustomEditor</code> needs its own name, which is why the example's button group sets <code>AriaLabel</code>; inside the
            group the arrow keys, Home and End move between the seasons.
        </p>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="demo/date-time">Date &amp; time</a>: the pickers the form items use for dates and times.</li>
            <li><a href="demo/checks">Checks &amp; switches</a>: the checkbox and switch editors.</li>
            <li><a href="demo/text-inputs">Text inputs</a>: the text box the form items use for strings and numbers.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

